<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Daniel O'Connell</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1775">1775</a>–<a href="/years/1847">1847</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Daniel O'Connell was an Irish political leader known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">the Liberator</a>. His Catholic Association organised mass, peaceful pressure that forced the British government to grant Catholic emancipation in 1829, and he then led a campaign for repeal of the Act of Union, which faltered after the government banned his monster meeting at Clontarf in 1843.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/daniel-oconnell.jpg" alt="Daniel O'Connell" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Mulrenin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Daniel_O%27Connell.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
